card.statement:
A Poisson vertex algebra (PVA) is a differential algebra $\mc V$ endowed with a $\lambda$-bracket which is skew-symmetric and satisfies the following Jacobi identity in $\mc V[\lambda,\mu]$ ($f,g,h\in\mc V$):

\begin{equation}
\{f_\lambda\{g_\mu h\}\}=
\{\{f_\lambda g\}_{\lambda+\mu}h\}+
\{g_\mu\{f_\lambda h\}\}\,.
\end{equation}
